{
  "summary": "Fixes wallet targeting errors in two functional tests. In wallet_keypool_topup.py, it backs up and restores each node's own wallet for nodes 1 through 4 rather than hardcoding node 1's paths, and adds an assertion that startup triggers a rescan. In wallet_createwallet.py, it tests the newly created w8 avoid_reuse wallet instead of inadvertently re-testing w7.",
  "problem": "Functional test coverage for keypool restore on p2sh-segwit, bech32, and bech32m output types was broken because nodes 2 through 4 never had their wallets replaced with backups, meaning the test passed trivially on untouched wallets. In wallet_createwallet.py, verifying that an unencrypted wallet created with avoid_reuse rejected walletpassphrase was skipped because the test invoked the RPC on the previous wallet handle.",
  "evidence": [
   "Description notes that wallet_keypool_topup.py copied node1's backup over node1's running wallet and restarted nodes 2-4 on their untouched wallets, leaving non-legacy keypool restoration untested since commit 0dcac51049.",
   "Description notes that adding an assertion for rescanning on master causes the test to fail immediately at node 2.",
   "Commit 13b2d21beb notes that since c5d3787367, wallet_createwallet.py called w7.walletpassphrase instead of w8, duplicating an existing assertion and failing to check the newly created avoid_reuse wallet."
